      "sequence_position": 14,
      "problem": "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b),$ if $b\\times c=⟨4,3,-5⟩$ and $a=⟨-2,8,2⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,8,2⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-5⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 4+8\\cdot 3+2\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-8+24-10 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
